{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-11-01T19:09:05.928699+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-01T19:09:06.131136+00:00", "id": 23865273, "conceptrecid": "23865272", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23865272", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "metadata": {"title": "Replication Package for \"Public Science, Business Research and the Conversion to Invention: A Three-Method Assessment of the European Knowledge Production Function\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "publication_date": "2026-11-01", "description": "<p>This package contains the data and code needed to reproduce the results of &ldquo;Public Science, Business Research and the Conversion to Invention: A Three-Method Assessment of the European Knowledge Production Function&rdquo; (Galiano, Dell&rsquo;Erba, Costantiello, Magazzino and Leogrande).</p>\n<p>The article estimates a knowledge production function for 36 European countries over 2017&ndash;2024 (288 country-years). PCT patent applications are the output; public and business R&amp;D, international and public&ndash;private co-publications and highly cited publications are the inputs. Three families of methods are applied to one specification:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>panel econometrics: pooled OLS, between, random effects, one- and two-way fixed effects, first differences and WLS, with a restricted wild cluster bootstrap, Driscoll&ndash;Kraay errors and Lewbel instruments;</li>\n<li>six clustering algorithms for the typology of innovation systems;</li>\n<li>five machine-learning learners used as a specification test, with leave-one-country-out validation, conditional permutation importance and accumulated local effects.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Contents:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data/</code>: the European Innovation Scoreboard 2024 database (European Commission) and two Eurostat datasets (rd_e_fundgerd, rd_e_gerdreg). All are public and included as downloaded.</li>\n<li><code>code/</code>: 39 Python scripts, one per analysis. Each writes its results to JSON or CSV.</li>\n<li><code>README.md</code>: instructions, sample definitions, estimation conventions, hyperparameters, random seeds and a map from each script to the tables and figures it produces.</li>\n<li><code>requirements.txt</code>: software versions (Python 3.13, NumPy 2.5, pandas 3.0, SciPy 1.18, statsmodels 0.15, scikit-learn 1.9).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Random seeds are fixed in every script; the baseline bootstrap uses seed 20261030 with 9,999 Rademacher replications. Run times range from seconds to about 30 minutes on two cores.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Galiano, Angelo Maurizio", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Dell'Erba, Giuseppe", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Costantiello, Alberto", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Magazzino, Cosimo", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Leogrande, Angelo", "affiliation": null}], "dates": [{"type": "available"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Computational notebook", "type": "software", "subtype": "computationalnotebook"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23865272"}}]}}, "title": "Replication Package for \"Public Science, Business Research and the Conversion to Invention: A Three-Method Assessment of the European Knowledge Production Function\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23865273", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23865273", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23865273?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23865273", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23865273/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23865272", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23865272", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23865272", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zeno