10.5281/zenodo.23862714", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23862713", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23862714", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Estimating Dynamics on Spatial Networks: An Application to Place-Based Policy Design\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23862714", "publication_date": "2026-11-01", "description": "<p>This replication package accompanies the paper &ldquo;Estimating Dynamics on Spatial Networks: An Application to Place-Based Policy Design&rdquo; by Davide Fiaschi, Angela Parenti and Cristiano Ricci.</p>\n<p>It provides R and Python code, input data and instructions for estimating a random vector field in Moran space using local-linear regression with adaptive bandwidths. The application studies population dynamics in more than 80,000 Italian grid cells connected by a fixed 2014 transport network and compares the resulting demographic taxonomy with Italy&rsquo;s National Strategy for Inner Areas (SNAI).</p>\n<p>The package includes data preparation, transport-network construction, spatial-block cross-validation, temporal validation, diagnostic checks, forward projections, network-sensitivity analysis, and scripts generating the paper&rsquo;s tables and figures. Software requirements, execution instructions and the scope of verification are documented in the README.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "FIASCHI, DAVIDE", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e0 di Pisa", "orcid": "0000-0002-1992-7071"}, {"name": "Parenti, Angela", "affiliation": "University of Pisa", "orcid": "0000-0002-5828-4291"}, {"name": "Ricci, Cristiano", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0003-4889-1474"}], "keywords": ["Nonparametric estimation; spatial networks; Moran space; random vector fields; population dynamics; place-based policies. spatial dependence"], "dates": [{"type": "submitted"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Computational notebook", "type": "software", "subtype": "computationalnotebook"}, "rel