026-10-31T10:01:24.020216+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-31T10:15:18.433319+00:00", "id": 23833406, "conceptrecid": "23833405", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23833406", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23833405", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23833406", "metadata": {"title": "Research materials for \"READING THE FINE PRINT: AI-ENABLED FRONTIER IN THE STUDY OF CONTRACTS\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23833406", "publication_date": "2026-10-31", "description": "<p>This deposit contains the research materials accompanying \"<strong>READING THE FINE PRINT: AI-ENABLED FRONTIER IN THE STUDY OF CONTRACTS\"</strong>, prepared for the <em>Organization Science</em> special issue AI-Enabled Frontiers in Organizational Science.</p>\n<p>It includes three components:&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>CoPA</strong>, a research tool for identifying contractual provisions and extracting contract-level information using language models accessed through APIs, with an editable, theory-derived codebook and instructions for users without programming experience</li>\n<li><strong>rep_package_CoPA_bench</strong>, a self-contained replication package containing the code, prompts, configurations, benchmark data, saved model predictions, and reported tables and figures for the CUAD evaluation, the meaning-preserving rewrite diagnostic, contract-level extraction, and the framing analysis</li>\n<li><strong>Org Sci SI_proposal_Appendix</strong>, the technical appendix explaining the methods, evaluation measures, and results.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The tool is intended for use with researchers&rsquo; own contracts, while the replication package documents its evaluation and an illustrative research application. Model inference requires API access and may incur charges.</p>\n<p>Author identities are omitted for anonymous review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relatio